{"title":"Career roadmap · Food Safety Officer","role":"Food Safety Officer","summary":"A Food Safety Officer (FSO) is responsible for enforcing food-safety regulations, inspecting food establishments, collecting samples, investigating violations, supporting food testing and ensuring compliance with food standards and hygiene requirements.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Food Science & Nutrition"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Food Science & Nutrition student, this is a relevant career direction, but government FSO eligibility is notification-specific. In India, eligibility can depend on the exact degree/subjects and the recruiting authority, so the student should verify the current notification before assuming that every B.Sc Food Science & Nutrition programme qualifies."},{"type":"h","text":"Career facts"},{"type":"table","header":["Item","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1"}],[{"text":"Current degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Food Science & Nutrition – General / Honours"}],[{"text":"Desired career"},{"text":"Food Safety Officer"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Food Safety · Public Health · Food Regulation"}],[{"text":"Primary route"},{"text":"B.Sc → eligibility/recruitment → Food Safety Officer"}],[{"text":"Strong advantage"},{"text":"Food microbiology + food chemistry + food law + inspection"}],[{"text":"Alternative route"},{"text":"Food QA/QC → Food Safety/Regulatory → Senior Food Safety roles"}],[{"text":"Higher qualification"},{"text":"M.Sc Food Science/Food Technology/Food Safety/Nutrition"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant, but recruitment eligibility must be checked carefully."},{"type":"p","text":"In India, Food Safety Officer positions are associated with the food-safety regulatory system under the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) and State/UT food-safety authorities."},{"type":"p","text":"The student should specifically verify whether their B.Sc Food Science & Nutrition curriculum and exact degree title satisfy the current FSO recruitment rules."},{"type":"p","text":"FSSAI is the primary official source for food-safety regulations and regulatory information.","url":"https://www.fssai.gov.in/"},{"type":"h","text":"Timeline assumption"},{"type":"p","text":"For a four-year B.Sc structure beginning in 2026, graduation would typically be around 2030. If the university follows a three-year B.Sc structure, compress the roadmap accordingly."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build food chemistry, microbiology, nutrition, food processing, hygiene and food-law fundamentals."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Pursue FSO recruitment where eligible or enter food QA/QC, food safety, auditing and regulatory roles."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Develop expertise in food inspection, risk assessment, HACCP, regulatory compliance, food testing and investigation."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward senior regulatory, food-safety management, policy, audit, technical or public-health leadership."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 – Sem 1"},{"text":"Biology, chemistry, nutrition and food fundamentals"},{"text":"University + laboratory"},{"text":"Food composition report"},{"text":"Scientific foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 – Sem 2"},{"text":"Food chemistry and human nutrition"},{"text":"Food chemistry lab"},{"text":"Food analysis practicals"},{"text":"Food knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 – Sem 1"},{"text":"Food microbiology and biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology lab"},{"text":"Microbial analysis report"},{"text":"Food microbiology"}]